# Vasilka, the Abbot's stitched bride (docs/voice/vasilka.md). on_the_table: unwoken, in the surgery at the end of the
# wards. never_woke: after the Abbot died before the rite. abandoned: left standing in the chapel in her dress.

~ on_the_table
Narrator: At the end of the old surgery, on a long table under a clean linen sheet, lies a young woman. The sheet is turned down to her collarbone, neatly, the way you'd tuck in a child.
Narrator: She is very beautiful. She does not breathe. Every so often, slowly, the fingers of her right hand close, as if around another hand, and then open again.
* [if not flag.vasilka_examined] [Medicine DC 12] (Look at her more closely.) -> examine_ok | examine_fail
* [if flag.vasilka_examined] (Look at her again.) -> again
* (Leave her.) -> END

~ examine_ok
set vasilka_examined
Narrator: The seams are finer than any surgeon's: wrists, throat, hairline. The left hand is older than the right; the eyes under the lids don't match. There is more than one woman here, and none of them is anyone any more.
interject class:cleric: These were Krezk's dead. Somebody's daughters. They were buried, with prayers said over them.
-> END

~ examine_fail
set vasilka_examined
Narrator: Pale skin, a careful hand with a needle somewhere in her past. She could be sleeping. You'd prefer she was sleeping.
-> END

~ again
if flag.abbot_dress_asked
Narrator: Somebody has laid out a pair of white slippers at the foot of the table, side by side, ready.
else
Narrator: Her hand closes. Opens. Closes.
endif
-> END

~ never_woke
Narrator: She lies under her linen as she always has. Nobody comes to turn the sheet down now, and dust has begun, very gently, to settle on her eyelashes.
* Cover her face. -> cover
* (Leave her.) -> END

~ cover
Narrator: You draw the sheet up over her face. It is the first thing in this house that has felt like a funeral.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You covered Vasilka's face
-> END

~ abandoned
Vasilka: Good evening. Is it time yet? Nobody has said. I am waiting very well. The Abbot said I was good at waiting.
* Lie down, Vasilka. Rest. -> rest
* (Leave her waiting.) -> END

~ rest
set vasilka_fate = "laid_to_rest"
Vasilka: Rest. Yes. I was very good at that, before.
Narrator: She lies down on the altar step and smooths her dress and closes her eyes, and does not open them again.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You told Vasilka she could rest
-> END
